# Project planning, step 2: tickets

A ticket is a piece of work. It extends the built-in TaskItem, so every ticket already has a status, a priority, dates, an estimate and someone it is assigned to, and every ticket appears on the kanban board.

The project gets a list of tickets.

```bss
t Project|upj
    A project: what you are delivering, broken down into tickets.
    s+                          Name|Project|A short name for the project
    s                           Description|Description|What the project will deliver, and why
    dd                          StartDate|Starts|When the project starts
    dd|(DueDate >= StartDate)   DueDate|Due|When the project should be finished
    l:uti                       Tickets|Tickets|The work in the project

x Ticket:TaskItem|uti
    A piece of work in a project.
```
